   * @x-autobe-specification Query todo_app_members table by primary key (id) matching the {memberId} path parameter. Include a LEFT JOIN with todo_app_profiles on todo_app_member_id to retrieve the display_name. Verify that the authenticated member's ID (extracted from the JWT token) matches the requested {memberId} — if they don't match, return a 403 Forbidden error. The SQL should select id, email, created_at, updated_at from members and display_name from profiles. Exclude password_hash and other internal fields. Return 404 Not Found if the member ID does not exist in the database. Use a single query with the join for efficiency.
